      "body": "### Search first\r\n\r\n- [X] I searched and no similar issues were found\r\n\r\n### What Happened?\r\n\r\nUsing Logseq 0.9.6 on Android 13 (Security patch May 2023), I want to host my Logseq graph on Nextcloud (locally hosted on my LAN).\r\n\r\nUsing the document browser I browse to nextcloud -> select the directory where my graph resides, but this returns me this error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nError: Cannot support this directory type: content://org.nextcloud.documents/tree/e481e080734577565209f10c88a78a12%2F197/document/e481e080734577565209f10c88a78a12%2F197\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/logseq/logseq/assets/5451787/b2b69baf-8070-4c1a-a607-879384d82f85)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Reproduce the Bug\r\n\r\n1. Start Logseq\r\n2. Go to \"All graphs\r\n3. \"Choose a folder\"\r\n4. Open from: Nextcloud (user@nextcloud.lan)\r\n5. Browse to directory\r\n6. Tap \"Use this folder\"\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nLogseq opens the folder and processes the graph\r\n\r\n### Screenshots\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Desktop or Mobile Platform Information\r\n\r\nLogseq 0.9.6\r\nAndroid 13 (sec patch may 2023)\r\nDevice: Samsung S22 Ultra\r\nNextcloud backend 25.0.6\r\nNextcloud client 3.24.2\r\n\r\n### Additional Context\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Are you willing to submit a PR? If you know how to fix the bug.\r\n\r\n- [ ] I'm willing to submit a PR (Thank you!)",
